NAME
    write - write words to a file

SYNOPSIS
    write <file> [words...]

DESCRIPTION
    Creates or overwrites <file> with the given words joined by single spaces
    (no trailing newline). With no words, truncates <file> to empty. For exact
    bytes or large content, use writeat or output redirection (> file).

EXAMPLES
    write hello.txt hello world
    ls -l > listing.txt

SEE ALSO
    writeat, cat, touch
